[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Now, we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and simplify.
