[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). This is a standard optimization problem where the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
