[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m The real part of this expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 324 \cos \theta + 504 \sin \theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m To maximize this expression, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = 504\), so the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 504^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 254016} = \sqrt{359000} = 18 \sqrt{1025}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2227203)[0m 
